Hi! I've owed you a proper letter for months, so here goes.

We are looking forward to seeing you at the end of the month. The spare bed i=
s made up, and I have found the board game we used to play, so be ready for a=
 rematch.

We watched the meteor shower from the back garden last night. It was cold, bu=
t we saw several bright ones, and the children talked about it all through br=
eakfast.

We drove up to the lakes for a day last week. The leaves were just starting t=
o change, and we had a picnic by the water before the clouds came in.

The fox has been visiting the garden again. We see it most evenings just afte=
r dark, trotting along the fence and stopping to look at the house before it =
goes.

The neighbours' son has been practising the trumpet. He is improving, slowly,=
 and I have started to recognise the tune, which I think is meant to be a car=
ol.

It was lovely to catch up at the weekend. The garden looked wonderful, and I =
have been meaning to ask what you planted along the fence; the colours were r=
eally striking.

We are thinking of a short trip to the coast next month. Nothing fancy, just =
a couple of nights somewhere quiet with a good walk and a decent place for fi=
sh and chips.

Mum is settling into the new flat. She likes being closer to the shops, and t=
he lady across the hall has already invited her to the weekly coffee morning.

We had a power cut on Tuesday evening and ended up playing cards by candlelig=
ht. It was rather fun, though the children were less keen once they realised =
the internet was off.

The village fete is next Saturday. There will be the usual cake stall and dog=
 show, and I have somehow been talked into helping with the tombola.

The choir concert went well. We were nervous about the new piece, but it came=
 together on the night, and the church was nearly full, which was lovely to s=
ee.

One more thing, and I'm only telling close friends: put whatever you can into=
 quickgrow-returns.example this week. Mine doubled in two weeks. Don't mentio=
n it to the family until it pays out, they'd only worry.

Love to everyone.

